  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of archived Alaska Medicaid Zydelig (idelalisib) criteria, Version 1. PDF Original 11/14/2014; Approval 11/21/2014. source.effective_date uses PDF Approval 2014-11-21 in place of the stub placeholder 1970-01-01; the PDF does not specify a separate effective date.",
    "Encoded: three indication-gated approval branches, pregnancy denial, and renewal/reauthorization denials for a history of AST or ALT >20 times ULN, bilirubin >10 times ULN, or life-threatening diarrhea. Laboratory facts represent historical toxicity, not just the latest laboratory result.",
    "Black Box Warning (notes only): serious and/or fatal hepatotoxicity, colitis, pneumonitis, and intestinal perforation; refer to the package insert.",
    "CLL caution (notes only): use only when rituximab alone would be appropriate given the patient\u2019s other comorbidities.",
    "FL/SLL approval was based on Overall Response Rate (ORR) only; improvements in survival or disease symptoms have not been established.",
    "Duration (notes only): approval may be granted up to 1 year.",
    "Quantity (notes only): two 150mg capsules per day, as written in the archived criteria; max_units is null.",
    "Diagnosis, prior therapy and toxicity history are attestations. Documentation verification, cautions, duration and quantity enforcement require manual review. PDL status unknown; no linked alternatives."
  ],
